Title: Swansea hosts UK's first ever IRONMAN Pro Series edition
Date: 2025-07-13
Firsthand information: {'Speaker': [{'Speaker': 'Harry Palmer', 'Text': '"It was hot, and I do feel for all the age-groupers who are out there today, because they\'ve got much harder conditions than we did, so fair play to everyone racing," Palmer told BBC Sport Wales.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 8, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 174}}, {'Speaker': 'Harry Palmer', 'Text': '"I didn\'t have the best swim, I\'ll be honest. I was in the second or third pack back, so I had some work to do on the bike.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 9, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 107}}, {'Speaker': 'Harry Palmer', 'Text': '"I came out [of the swim] with the likes of Will Crudgington, Freddie Webb, Malachi Cashmore, some other boys, and Kristian Høgenhaug, who was one of the guys I was keeping an eye on.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 10, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 164}}, {'Speaker': 'Harry Palmer', 'Text': '"He\'s an epic rider who likes to get on the front of the bike, so I felt I was in good company.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 11, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 90}}, {'Speaker': 'Harry Palmer', 'Text': '"My favourite part is the support.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 12, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 32}}, {'Speaker': 'Harry Palmer', 'Text': '"The course is amazing, especially with weather like this, and the Gower is incredible.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 13, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 80}}, {'Speaker': 'Harry Palmer', 'Text': '"But it\'s the people — it\'s the Welsh. They just know how to put on an event and how to support. I\'ll keep coming back to Welsh events because of that."', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 14, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 135}}, {'Speaker': 'Kat Matthews', 'Text': '"Three years feels like a lifetime. A lot has happened since then," Matthews, who last won in Swansea in 2022, said.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 18, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 100}}, {'Speaker': 'Kat Matthews', 'Text': '"I feel like a completely different person, and it felt like a different event this time around.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 19, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 88}}, {'Speaker': 'Kat Matthews', 'Text': '"I didn\'t have as much deficit coming out of the swim as I expected, so I was really motivated to attack at the start of the bike and catch the girls at the front.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 20, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 142}}, {'Speaker': 'Kat Matthews', 'Text': '"I was happy to see them quite quickly and pull them back, but then suddenly I was on my own at the front. It was quite nice to feel in control until the run, when I felt a bit hot."', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 21, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 163}}, {'Speaker': 'Race Director Rebecca Sutherland', 'Text': '"It\'s always great fun when we go racing in Swansea, and this year was no different.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 25, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 79}}, {'Speaker': 'Race Director Rebecca Sutherland', 'Text': '"It was another incredible race with thousands of athletes crossing the famous red carpet finish line to rapturous spectator support."', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 26, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 129}}], 'Description': [{'Description': 'With air temperatures soaring above 28°C, and water temperatures exceeding 24°C, race organisers ruled the professional swim non-wetsuit, as it surpassed the wetsuit-legal limit.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 4, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 165}}, {'Description': 'It marked the first time elite athletes in the Ironman Pro Series have raced under such conditions in the UK.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 5, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 88}}, {'Description': 'Defending champion Palmer claimed back-to-back victories in Swansea, taking the overall Pro Series win in a time of 3:51:18.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 6, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 118}}, {'Description': "Just 49 seconds separated him from training partner, France's Leon Chevalier as fellow Brit Kieran Lindars claimed third place.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 7, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 110}}, {'Description': 'Overall Ironman Pro Series 2024 winner Matthews, claimed victory in Swansea with a time of 4:20:37.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 15, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 93}}, {'Description': "Britain's Rebecca Anderbury and Danila Kleiser of Germany completed the podium, finishing second and third in the female professional race respectively.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 16, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 129}}, {'Description': 'Thousands of supporters and volunteers lined the 70-mile course, providing encouragement and welfare support throughout the day.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 22, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 110}}, {'Description': 'With over half of the age-group field tackling their first IRONMAN 70.3, it was a day to remember for both competitors and their families.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 23, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 115}}, {'Description': 'The race is set to return to the coastal city next summer for the fourth edition of the event.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 27, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 87}}], 'Image': [{'ID': 'image_1', 'Caption': 'Kat Matthews breaks the tape in Swansea to take home the maximum amount of Pro Series points.'}]}
